{"id": "EUVD-2026-76581", "enisaUuid": "5db6aa9a-8178-3d95-a662-0b18950fb7b4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: initialize copy-notify stateid before publishing it\n\nnfsd4_copy_notify() finished initializing the cpntf state after\nnfs4_alloc_init_cpntf_state() had already linked it into the\ns2s_cp_stateids IDR and the parent's sc_cp_list, with cs_count == 1 (the\nmembership reference) and none held for the caller. A racing\nOFFLOAD_CANCEL (crafted cl_id == nn->s2s_cp_cl_id plus the guessable\nso_id) could reach manage_cpntf_state() and free the entry, turning the\ncaller's subsequent cpn_cnr_stateid read and cp_p_stateid/cp_p_clid\nwrites into use-after-free. The owning clientid was also only recorded\nafter publication, so it could not gate an ownership check in that window.\n\nRecord cp_p_stateid and cp_p_clid inside nfs4_alloc_init_cpntf_state()\nbefore nfs4_init_cp_state() publishes the entry, and return it with an\nextra reference. The caller reads the stateid under that reference and\ndrops it with nfs4_put_cpntf_state(); on a late error the laundromat\nreaps the entry.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:50:42", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/863b6e995665472f2af5be2436a874ab6a9e5ac6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d18d36395d973ef7372c8e6724970585f75b5c0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4415a692346a39fdb647cbd717eda510159aaf55", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9caad13b7cfe9ccb90cc405ac77335800e086595", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e08a3dcaca0505f861e344a387f37f94d95dbdc2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a4d7fedcaaf33e60a01e53eafca9041ef966212f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cdef96892f4fa6e70c405b6e8f2fd6972f3b64b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/129643893b79f8a3c6b72045f933fbab5ee424ca"], "aliases": ["GHSA-76rg-3h22-jw6r", "CVE-2026-89669"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.69, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16e92afd-f48e-3318-9e05-c1da4a744c32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "624322f1adc58acd0b69f77a6ddc764207e97241 <d18d36395d973ef7372c8e6724970585f75b5c0b"}, {"id": "17cc4cc7-304d-3ee5-8d27-12a837b3fe03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "624322f1adc58acd0b69f77a6ddc764207e97241 <a4d7fedcaaf33e60a01e53eafca9041ef966212f"}, {"id": "1c72aa09-0354-363c-a758-bbe01415c2dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "1f80067d-884b-352e-bbe0-1be3f0a7a05e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "624322f1adc58acd0b69f77a6ddc764207e97241 <9caad13b7cfe9ccb90cc405ac77335800e086595"}, {"id": "249d26f8-df72-34e9-a120-ee3f08655001", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "2793038c-e3f1-3b31-8489-106478e43478", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "3c2bd212-c12b-3f37-8244-a46e7986f8f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "624322f1adc58acd0b69f77a6ddc764207e97241 <e08a3dcaca0505f861e344a387f37f94d95dbdc2"}, {"id": "542dc997-ce4d-339c-9c46-28e5819e8e91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "624322f1adc58acd0b69f77a6ddc764207e97241 <4415a692346a39fdb647cbd717eda510159aaf55"}, {"id": "67a2fbfb-eebf-3176-85e7-641f121f0624", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8686a673-0ff7-3baa-b82f-adfb157a8335", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "92171169-d632-35e3-855e-ec711f5d95af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "624322f1adc58acd0b69f77a